  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "The idea is simple.",
      "start_ms": 0,
      "end_ms": 1280,
      "start_frame": 0,
      "end_frame": 38,
      "word_count": 4
    },
    {
      "text": "For every string, write its length, then a hash, then the original string.",
      "start_ms": 1580,
      "end_ms": 7760,
      "start_frame": 47,
      "end_frame": 233,
      "word_count": 13
    },
    {
      "text": "So our record format becomes length, hash, payload.",
      "start_ms": 8380,
      "end_ms": 12580,
      "start_frame": 251,
      "end_frame": 377,
      "word_count": 8
    },
    {
      "text": "The hash ends the length header.",
      "start_ms": 13580,
      "end_ms": 15480,
      "start_frame": 407,
      "end_frame": 464,
      "word_count": 6
    },
    {
      "text": "After that, the decoder reads exactly the specified number of characters.",
      "start_ms": 16540,
      "end_ms": 21240,
      "start_frame": 496,
      "end_frame": 637,
      "word_count": 11
    },
    {
      "text": "Even if the payload contains a hash, it is safe.",
      "start_ms": 22160,
      "end_ms": 26220,
      "start_frame": 665,
      "end_frame": 787,
      "word_count": 10
    },
    {
      "text": "And after each record, the pointer, I must reach the next length header.",
      "start_ms": 27140,
      "end_ms": 32160,
      "start_frame": 814,
      "end_frame": 965,
      "word_count": 13
    },
    {
      "text": "That's the protocol.",
      "start_ms": 33160,
      "end_ms": 34280,
      "start_frame": 995,
      "end_frame": 1028,
      "word_count": 3
    },
    {
      "text": "Now let's encode our full example.",
      "start_ms": 35080,
      "end_ms": 37240,
      "start_frame": 1052,
      "end_frame": 1117,
      "word_count": 6
    }
  ],
